    "scope": "Complete mapped granary/Житня exterior at Yasnaya Polyana: timber-supported two-storey storehouse with log lower walls, weathered vertical-board upper room, broad low hip roof over an open front gallery and an external stair descending along the front. Lower double wooden gate and upper doorway are physically recessed; short-side vent, timber posts, open rails, stringers and supported entrance/foot aprons remain simple original proxies. All four mapped outer edges anchor the house/gallery envelope. Hidden rear inventory, roof material and historic levels remain approximate. No copied signs, merchandise, inscriptions, artworks, furnishings, people, snow or photograph pixels.",
    "identityBasis": "Museum granary/Житня corresponds to way220075392, independent of the other estate houses and the separate riga. Exact13m by6.9m map outline anchors the envelope; the enclosed front wall is set back1.1m to leave the photo-visible gallery inside that outline. X northwest along the long front, Z northeast toward the approach; native east/up/south axes baked with heading0 at the unchanged assigned member anchor. Autumn end/front and winter front museum photos guide the open gallery, external stair and timber wall hierarchy; hidden faces and absolute front assignment remain an approximate map/photo interpretation.",
    "heightBasis": "Photo-led approximate medium-fi scale: lower room2.25m, upper room2.05m, low hip roof1.5m rise. Gallery at2.25m has simple.92m open rails;12 treads descend along the front. Map nominal5m is a scale cue. Rear bays, historical cladding/roof state, timber frame sections, doors, treads, thresholds and accessibility are not surveyed.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retained Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen201x201/6m ground; outside northeast approach provider[0,7] supplies224.57842704651677m datum. Boundary grades-0.993..0.254m, floor+0.5m and timber pier bottoms-1.2m. The coarse slope leaves up to about1.5m below the downhill floor; the original ground remains beneath the raised rooms, gallery and stair. Only occupied pier feet and the two supported aprons cut the ground. Historic support exposure/levels and accessibility approximate; no flattening or bespoke terrain. Independent neighbors, approaches, roads and ponds remain."
